# Jetson Build Configuration Guide
# =============================================================================
# For building on/for Jetson Orin NX or Jetson Orin Nano
# =============================================================================

# BUILD ON JETSON DEVICE (Recommended)
# ====================================
# This is the recommended approach as JetPack is optimized for the device

# 1. Ensure your Jetson has:
#    - JetPack 6.0+ (includes ROS2 Humble, CUDA 12.2, cuDNN 8.x)
#    - Docker with nvidia-docker runtime

# 2. Clone the repository on Jetson:
#    git clone <your-repo> /workspaces/isaac_ros-dev/stereo-slam-3Dmapping

# 3. Build the Docker image (on Jetson):
#    cd /workspaces/isaac_ros-dev/stereo-slam-3Dmapping
#    docker build -f docker/Dockerfile.mine -t stereo-slam:jetson-orin-nx .

# 4. Run container with GPU access:
#    docker run --rm --runtime nvidia \
#      -v /workspaces/isaac_ros-dev:/workspaces/isaac_ros-dev \
#      -v /dev:/dev \
#      --device-cgroup-rule='c 241:* rmw' \
#      -it stereo-slam:jetson-orin-nx /bin/bash

# BUILD CROSS-COMPILE (Advanced, not recommended)
# ================================================
# If you need to build on x86_64 for Jetson deployment:
# - Use qemu-user-static for cross-compilation
# - May have performance/compatibility issues
# - Not recommended - better to build natively on Jetson

# DEPLOYMENT CHECKLIST
# ====================
# Before running on Jetson:
# 
# [ ] Jetson device: Orin NX or Orin Nano confirmed
# [ ] JetPack version: 6.0+ with ROS2 Humble
# [ ] Available storage: 50GB+ for models + workspace
# [ ] Available GPU memory: 8GB (Orin NX) or 4GB (Orin Nano)
# [ ] CUDA compute capability: 8.7 (Orin NX) or 8.7 (Orin Nano)
# 
# Performance constraints:
# - Orin NX: 8-core ARM CPU, 8GB unified memory, 100 TOPS peak
# - Orin Nano: 6-core ARM CPU, 4GB/8GB unified memory, 40 TOPS peak
# - Both suitable for full GPU pipeline (ESS + VSLAM + Nvblox)
# - May need to reduce buffer pool size (ess_params.yaml threshold)

# RUNTIME OPTIMIZATION FOR JETSON
# ================================
# Set these environment variables before running:
#
# export NVPMODEL_CONFIG_FILE=/etc/nvpmodel.conf
# export JETSON_CLOCKS_ENABLED=0  # Set to 1 for max performance (higher power)
# export CUDA_FORCE_PTX_JIT=0     # Use cached kernels instead of JIT
# export RMW_IMPLEMENTATION=rmw_cyclonedds_cpp  # Faster DDS implementation
# export CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0   # Specify which GPU to use (0 on Jetson)

# MEMORY CONSTRAINTS
# ==================
# Jetson Orin Nano 4GB example:
# - OS + Docker + ROS2: ~1.5GB
# - Model files (ESS): ~500MB
# - Pipeline buffers (8x): ~200-300MB
# - Available for processing: ~1-1.5GB (tight!)
#
# Recommendations:
# - Use num_buffers=4 instead of 8 for Nano 4GB
# - Reduce image resolution if needed (resize_params.yaml)
# - Monitor GPU memory with: nvidia-smi -l 1

# BUILD COMMANDS
# ==============

# 1. Build on native Jetson (BEST):
#    docker build -f docker/Dockerfile.mine \
#      --build-arg BASE_IMAGE=nvcr.io/nvidia/isaac/ros:jetson-orin-ros2_humble \
#      -t stereo-slam:jetson-orin-nx .

# 2. Run with GPU + device access:
#    docker run --rm --runtime nvidia \
#      -e NVIDIA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=all \
#      -e CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0 \
#      --device /dev/nvhost-ctrl \
#      --device /dev/nvhost-ctrl-gp1 \
#      --device /dev/nvhost-gpu \
#      --device /dev/nvmap \
#      -v /workspaces/isaac_ros-dev:/workspaces/isaac_ros-dev \
#      -it stereo-slam:jetson-orin-nx bash

# 3. Inside container, build workspace:
#    cd /workspaces/isaac_ros-dev
#    colcon build --symlink-install --cmake-args \
#      -DCMAKE_CXX_STANDARD=17 \
#      -DCMAKE_CXX_FLAGS="-O3 -march=native"

# 4. Run pipeline:
#    source install/setup.bash
#    export BAG_PATH=/path/to/rosbag
#    ./scripts/run_full_pipeline.bash --use_sim_time:=true

# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ===============
# 
# "Out of memory" errors:
#   - Reduce num_buffers in launch file (currently 8)
#   - Set JETSON_CLOCKS_ENABLED=0 to reduce power/thermal but gain headroom
#   - Check nvidia-smi for memory pressure
#
# "CUDA out of memory":
#   - ESS model too large: check ess_params.yaml engine path
#   - Reduce resolution: adjust resize_params.yaml
#   - Close other GPU processes
#
# "Port already in use":
#   - TCP endpoint port (10000): change in launch file
#   - Foxglove port (8765): change in Foxglove config
#
# "TF transforms missing":
#   - Check rosbag has /kevin/tf topic
#   - Run diagnose_tf.bash to debug frame tree
